## Pre-delivery checklists

### Every interactive component

- [ ] Keyboard operable; visible focus ring (≥2px, ≥3:1 contrast against adjacent colors)
- [ ] Focus not fully obscured by sticky headers, modals, or sheets (2.4.11)
- [ ] Accessible name matches visible label (2.5.3); `aria-label` only when no visible label
- [ ] Role, name, value, and state exposed (4.1.2); disabled/expanded/checked announced
- [ ] Touch/click target ≥24×24 CSS px (2.5.8); prefer 44×44 (2.5.5 AAA)
- [ ] Color not sole indicator of state — add icon, text, pattern, or border (1.4.1, 1.3.3)
- [ ] Text contrast ≥4.5:1 (normal), ≥3:1 (large text ≥18pt/14pt bold) (1.4.3)
- [ ] UI control boundaries ≥3:1 against background (1.4.11)
- [ ] Motion/animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion` (2.3.3 AAA)
- [ ] No seizure-inducing flash >3/sec (2.3.1)

### Every page / screen / Figma frame

- [ ] Unique, descriptive `<title>` / frame name (2.4.2)
- [ ] Logical heading hierarchy (`h1`→`h2`→…); one `h1` per view (1.3.1, 2.4.6)
- [ ] Skip link or landmark to main content (2.4.1)
- [ ] `lang` on root; `lang` on foreign-language passages (3.1.1, 3.1.2)
- [ ] Focus order matches visual/reading order (2.4.3)
- [ ] Consistent nav, help, and component identification across pages (3.2.3, 3.2.4, 3.2.6)
- [ ] Reflows at 320px width / 400% zoom without horizontal scroll (1.4.10)
- [ ] Status messages use `role="status"` / `role="alert"` / `aria-live` (4.1.3)
- [ ] Tooltips/popovers: dismissable (Esc), hoverable, persistent until dismissed (1.4.13)

### Every form

- [ ] Visible `<label>` linked via `for`/`id` or wrapping (3.3.2, 1.3.1)
- [ ] `autocomplete` tokens on personal data fields (1.3.5)
- [ ] Errors identified in text, linked to fields via `aria-describedby` (3.3.1)
- [ ] Correction suggestions where possible (3.3.3)
- [ ] Legal/financial/data submissions: reversible, validated, or confirmed (3.3.4)
- [ ] Do not re-ask for data already entered in same session (3.3.7)
- [ ] Auth: allow paste, password managers; no cognitive puzzles without alternative (3.3.8)

### Design tokens (this design system)

- [ ] Semantic color tokens meet contrast pairs (text/background, control/border)
- [ ] Focus ring tokens: visible in light and dark appearance modes
- [ ] Minimum spacing tokens support 24px+ targets and text-spacing overrides (1.4.12)
- [ ] Motion tokens gated behind reduced-motion preference in CSS

