## WCAG 2.2 — all 86 active success criteria

Criterion **4.1.1 Parsing** was removed in WCAG 2.2. All others below are active.

### Principle 1 — Perceivable

#### 1.1 Text alternatives
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 1.1.1 | A | Non-text content has text alternative | `alt` on images; `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` on icon-only controls; decorative images `alt=""` + `aria-hidden="true"` |

#### 1.2 Time-based media
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 1.2.1 | A | Audio/video alternatives | Transcript for audio; transcript or audio-described version for video |
| 1.2.2 | A | Captions (prerecorded) | Synchronized captions on prerecorded video |
| 1.2.3 | A | Audio description or alternative | Audio description track or text alternative describing visuals |
| 1.2.4 | AA | Captions (live) | Live captioning for live audio |
| 1.2.5 | AA | Audio description (prerecorded) | Audio description for prerecorded video |
| 1.2.6 | AAA | Sign language | Sign language interpretation |
| 1.2.7 | AAA | Extended audio description | Pause video for extended descriptions when needed |
| 1.2.8 | AAA | Media alternative | Full text document equivalent for prerecorded media |
| 1.2.9 | AAA | Audio-only (live) | Live text alternative for live audio-only |

#### 1.3 Adaptable
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 1.3.1 | A | Info and relationships | Semantic HTML: `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<table>`, `<th scope>`, fieldset/legend for groups |
| 1.3.2 | A | Meaningful sequence | DOM order = reading order; CSS must not break sequence |
| 1.3.3 | A | Sensory characteristics | "Click the red button" → add "Submit" label; don't rely on shape/position/sound alone |
| 1.3.4 | AA | Orientation | No lock to portrait/landscape unless essential |
| 1.3.5 | AA | Identify input purpose | `autocomplete="email"`, `tel`, `name`, `street-address`, etc. |
| 1.3.6 | AAA | Identify purpose | `aria-label` with purpose tokens; schema.org/microdata where applicable |

#### 1.4 Distinguishable
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 1.4.1 | A | Use of color | Pair color with text, icon, or pattern for errors, links, charts, states |
| 1.4.2 | A | Audio control | Auto-playing audio >3s: provide pause/stop/mute |
| 1.4.3 | AA | Contrast (minimum) | **4.5:1** normal text; **3:1** large text (≥24px or ≥18.66px bold) |
| 1.4.4 | AA | Resize text | 200% zoom: no loss of content/function (use rem/em, avoid fixed px heights on text containers) |
| 1.4.5 | AA | Images of text | Use real text + web fonts; images of text only when essential |
| 1.4.6 | AAA | Contrast (enhanced) | **7:1** normal text; **4.5:1** large text |
| 1.4.7 | AAA | Low background audio | Speech foreground 20dB louder than background |
| 1.4.8 | AAA | Visual presentation | User can set width, spacing, colors (no !important blocking overrides) |
| 1.4.9 | AAA | Images of text (no exception) | No images of text except logo/essential |
| 1.4.10 | AA | Reflow | 320 CSS px width at 400% zoom: single column, no horizontal scroll for vertical content |
| 1.4.11 | AA | Non-text contrast | Icons, borders, focus rings, chart lines: **3:1** against adjacent colors |
| 1.4.12 | AA | Text spacing | Survive user overrides: line-height 1.5×, paragraph spacing 2×, letter-spacing 0.12em, word-spacing 0.16em |
| 1.4.13 | AA | Content on hover/focus | Additional content (tooltip): dismissable (Esc), pointer can move to content, stays until dismissed/hover removed |

### Principle 2 — Operable

#### 2.1 Keyboard accessible
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 2.1.1 | A | Keyboard | All functionality via keyboard; no `onClick`-only without `onKeyDown` equivalent |
| 2.1.2 | A | No keyboard trap | Focus can leave modals (Esc, close button, focus trap with exit) |
| 2.1.3 | AAA | Keyboard (no exception) | No exceptions to keyboard access |
| 2.1.4 | A | Character key shortcuts | Single-key shortcuts (e.g. `j`): provide disable/remap or active-only-when-focused |

#### 2.2 Enough time
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 2.2.1 | A | Timing adjustable | Session timeouts: warn + extend; carousels: pause control |
| 2.2.2 | A | Pause, stop, hide | Moving/blinking/auto-updating content >5s: user can pause/stop/hide |
| 2.2.3 | AAA | No timing | No time limits except real-time events (auctions) |
| 2.2.4 | AAA | Interruptions | Defer non-urgent interruptions; user can postpone |
| 2.2.5 | AAA | Re-authenticating | Preserve data after re-auth |
| 2.2.6 | AAA | Timeouts | Warn users before data loss from inactivity |

#### 2.3 Seizures
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 2.3.1 | A | Three flashes | No content flashing >3 times/sec above thresholds |
| 2.3.2 | AAA | Three flashes | Stricter flash limits |
| 2.3.3 | AAA | Animation from interactions | Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`; provide off switch |

#### 2.4 Navigable
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 2.4.1 | A | Bypass blocks | `<a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>` + `<main id="main">` |
| 2.4.2 | A | Page titled | Unique `<title>` describing page purpose |
| 2.4.3 | A | Focus order | `tabIndex` only on interactive elements; order matches visual flow |
| 2.4.4 | A | Link purpose (in context) | Link text + context = destination; avoid "click here" |
| 2.4.5 | AA | Multiple ways | Nav + search + sitemap for multi-page sites |
| 2.4.6 | AA | Headings and labels | Headings describe sections; labels describe inputs |
| 2.4.7 | AA | Focus visible | Never `outline: none` without custom focus style |
| 2.4.8 | AAA | Location | Breadcrumbs or "you are here" indicator |
| 2.4.9 | AAA | Link purpose (link only) | Link text alone describes destination |
| 2.4.10 | AAA | Section headings | Organize content with headings |
| 2.4.11 | AA | **Focus not obscured (min)** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — Sticky bars/sheets must not fully hide focused element |
| 2.4.12 | AAA | **Focus not obscured (enhanced)** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — No part of focused element hidden |
| 2.4.13 | AAA | **Focus appearance** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — Focus indicator: ≥2px perimeter, ≥3:1 contrast change |

#### 2.5 Input modalities
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 2.5.1 | A | Pointer gestures | Pinch/swipe/multi-finger: provide single-pointer alternative |
| 2.5.2 | A | Pointer cancellation | Use `click` event (up-event), not `mousedown` alone |
| 2.5.3 | A | Label in name | Visible "Search" → `aria-label` must contain "Search" |
| 2.5.4 | A | Motion actuation | Shake/tilt triggers: provide UI alternative + disable option |
| 2.5.5 | AAA | Target size (enhanced) | **44×44 CSS px** minimum |
| 2.5.6 | AAA | Concurrent input mechanisms | Don't disable keyboard when touch is available |
| 2.5.7 | AA | **Dragging movements** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — Sliders/drag-drop: provide tap/click alternative |
| 2.5.8 | AA | **Target size (minimum)** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — **24×24 CSS px** minimum (or 24px spacing to another target) |

### Principle 3 — Understandable

#### 3.1 Readable
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 3.1.1 | A | Language of page | `<html lang="en">` |
| 3.1.2 | AA | Language of parts | `<span lang="de">` on foreign phrases |
| 3.1.3 | AAA | Unusual words | Glossary for jargon |
| 3.1.4 | AAA | Abbreviations | Expand abbreviations on first use or via mechanism |
| 3.1.5 | AAA | Reading level | Supplemental plain-language summary for complex text |
| 3.1.6 | AAA | Pronunciation | Ruby/phonetic for ambiguous words |

#### 3.2 Predictable
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 3.2.1 | A | On focus | Focus alone does not navigate or submit |
| 3.2.2 | A | On input | Changing input does not auto-navigate without warning |
| 3.2.3 | AA | Consistent navigation | Same nav order/position across pages |
| 3.2.4 | AA | Consistent identification | Same icon/label for same function everywhere |
| 3.2.5 | AAA | Change on request | Context changes only on explicit user action |
| 3.2.6 | A | **Consistent help** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — Help/contact links in same relative position across pages |

#### 3.3 Input assistance
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 3.3.1 | A | Error identification | Describe error in text; `aria-invalid="true"` |
| 3.3.2 | A | Labels or instructions | Every input has visible label + hint text when needed |
| 3.3.3 | AA | Error suggestion | "Email must include @" not just "Invalid" |
| 3.3.4 | AA | Error prevention (legal/financial/data) | Confirm step, review screen, or undo for critical actions |
| 3.3.5 | AAA | Help | Context-sensitive help available |
| 3.3.6 | AAA | Error prevention (all) | Confirm/review for all submissions |
| 3.3.7 | A | **Redundant entry** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — Auto-fill from prior entries in same process |
| 3.3.8 | AA | **Accessible authentication (min)** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — Allow paste + password managers; no memory puzzles without alternative |
| 3.3.9 | AAA | **Accessible authentication (enhanced)** | **WCAG 2.2 NEW** — No object-recognition or user-supplied image CAPTCHAs |

### Principle 4 — Robust

#### 4.1 Compatible
| ID | Lvl | Rule | Implementation |
|----|-----|------|----------------|
| 4.1.2 | A | Name, role, value | Native controls preferred; custom widgets need ARIA roles/states |
| 4.1.3 | AA | Status messages | Toast/validation banners: `role="status"` or `aria-live="polite"` |

