## European Accessibility Act (EAA) — additional requirements

Beyond WCAG, the EAA (Directive 2019/882) imposes **functional** obligations. Flag these when relevant to the product scope.

### EAA scope (digital products & services in EU market)

Applies to e-commerce, consumer banking, telecommunications, transport booking, e-books, and related hardware/software interfaces. Design system components built for these contexts must meet EAA from the start.

### EAA functional requirements (Article 4)

| Requirement | What to enforce |
|-------------|-----------------|
| **Perceivable** | Information presented in usable formats for users with visual, auditory, speech, and cognitive disabilities |
| **Operable** | UI operable via assistive tech and alternative input; no unnecessary barriers |
| **Understandable** | Clear language, predictable behaviour, input assistance |
| **Robust** | Compatible with assistive technologies; valid, semantic markup |
| **Consistent & adequate** | Websites and apps accessible in a **consistent** way across the service |

### EAA service-specific (flag for product teams)

| Area | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| **E-commerce** | Product info, checkout, payment, order tracking — all WCAG 2.2 AA + clear error recovery |
| **Consumer banking** | Account info, transactions, authentication — enhanced error prevention (3.3.4) |
| **Help & support** | Help desks, call centres, and training must provide accessibility information (offline channels too) |
| **Documentation** | Technical documentation describing accessibility features |
| **Accessibility statement** | Public statement of conformance, contact for feedback, enforcement procedure link (per national law) |
| **Non-digital components** | ATMs, terminals, hardware — physical operability (out of scope for web DS, but flag if designing kiosk UI) |

### EN 301 549 alignment

- Web content: conform to **WCAG 2.2 Level AA** (exceeds current EN 301 549 WCAG 2.1 reference).
- Software (mobile/desktop): same WCAG criteria apply to web views; native apps follow platform accessibility APIs.
- Documentation: provide conformance evidence (test results, VPAT/ACR where applicable).

